WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.709
First, launch Copilot.

00:00:02.709 --> 00:00:04.618
Loading is sped up.

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:10.295
Type /autopilot, followed by your goal.

00:00:10.295 --> 00:00:13.920
Here: fix all TypeScript errors in the source folder.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:19.475
It first asks which permission mode to use.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.405
We choose Allow All, so it can work uninterrupted.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:26.743
Copilot is now locked onto the goal.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:32.182
It defines success: zero TypeScript errors, with the build and lint passing.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:39.243
Then it inspects the project: the git status, the TypeScript config, and the source files.

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:47.845
And it keeps going until the objective is met.

00:00:47.845 --> 00:00:50.902
Think of it like setting a GPS destination.
